		{"text": "REVIEWS AND COMMENTARY", "rect": [443.85227550159794, 763.5909139459782, 542.6136328957297, 772.5909118652343], "fontSize": 8.999997919256089},
		{"text": "•", "rect": [544.6249944513493, 764.5795482288706, 547.0795336636629, 771.5795454545454], "fontSize": 6.999997225674747},
		{"text": "REVIEW", "rect": [553.2954545454544, 763.5909139459782, 579.7386412187055, 772.5909118652343], "fontSize": 8.999997919256089},
		{"text": "This copy is for personal use only. To order copies, contact", "rect": [160.27271617542613, 9.443200544877461, 372.72726579145944, 18.44319846413353], "fontSize": 8.999997919256069},
		{"text": "reprints@rsna.org", "rect": [375.79546841708094, 9.443200544877461, 441.0000124844637, 18.44319846413353], "fontSize": 8.999997919256069},
		{"text": "T", "rect": [71.96590076793323, 406.7613435225053, 87.13635531338777, 431.95452325994313], "fontSize": 25.193179737437845},
		{"text": "he operational efficiency of CT, combined with its spa-", "rect": [80.4659063165838, 421.7954781272194, 291.31817904385645, 431.7954711914062], "fontSize": 9.99999306418681},
		{"text": "tial and contrast resolution, has made CT the preferred", "rect": [80.4659063165838, 409.81817488236857, 291.31817904385645, 419.8181679465554], "fontSize": 9.99999306418681},
		{"text": "modality in patient assessment for a wide variety of pedi-", "rect": [71.96590076793323, 397.84091325239694, 291.3295399058948, 407.84090631658376], "fontSize": 9.99999306418681},
		{"text": "atric conditions, including trauma, lung disease, and bone", "rect": [71.96590076793323, 385.79543443159616, 291.35226162997157, 395.7954378995028], "fontSize": 10.000003467906652},
		{"text": "abnormalities in neurologic and musculoskeletal diseases.", "rect": [71.96590076793323, 373.8181728016246, 291.3409007679332, 383.8181762695312], "fontSize": 10.000003467906595},
		{"text": "The use of CT in pediatric imaging compared with adult", "rect": [71.96590076793323, 361.8409215753728, 291.4090659401633, 371.8409146395596], "fontSize": 9.99999306418681},
		{"text": "imaging prioritizes radiation dose reduction and minimi-", "rect": [71.96590076793323, 349.78408189253366, 291.3409007679332, 359.78408536044026], "fontSize": 10.000003467906595},
		{"text": "zation of motion artifacts for a population who may be", "rect": [71.96590076793323, 337.8068306662819, 291.36362249200994, 347.8068237304687], "fontSize": 9.99999306418681},
		{"text": "more sensitive to ionizing radiation and who may require", "rect": [71.96590076793323, 325.8295690363103, 291.35226162997157, 335.82956210049707], "fontSize": 9.999993064186754},
		{"text": "sedation and general anesthesia for diagnostic examina-", "rect": [71.96590076793323, 313.85226579145944, 291.36362249200994, 323.85225885564626], "fontSize": 9.99999306418681},
		{"text": "tions. The technical features of photon-counting detector", "rect": [71.96590076793323, 301.80682858553797, 291.4090659401633, 311.80683205344457], "fontSize": 10.000003467906595},
		{"text": "(PCD) CT over conventional energy-integrating detector", "rect": [71.96590076793323, 289.8295253406871, 291.43180847167963, 299.8295288085937], "fontSize": 10.000003467906595},
		{"text": "(EID) CT are tailored to optimize radiation dose reduc-", "rect": [71.96590076793323, 277.85226371071553, 291.39770507812494, 287.8522671786221], "fontSize": 10.000003467906595},
		{"text": "tion. The currently approved PCD CT system, which uses", "rect": [71.96590076793323, 265.8750124844638, 291.39770507812494, 275.8750055486505], "fontSize": 9.999993064186697},
		{"text": "a dual-source geometry, also features scan speeds compa-", "rect": [71.96590076793323, 253.8181728016246, 291.36362249200994, 263.81817626953125], "fontSize": 10.000003467906652},
		{"text": "rable with those of previous third-generation dual-source", "rect": [71.96590076793323, 241.85227203369135, 291.39770507812494, 251.85227550159797], "fontSize": 10.000003467906623},
		{"text": "scanners, but with a new capacity to scan at maximum", "rect": [71.96590076793323, 229.87501040371978, 291.3295399058948, 239.8750138716264], "fontSize": 10.000003467906623},
		{"text": "speed while acquiring multienergy data and images at", "rect": [71.96590076793323, 217.8977071588689, 291.36362249200994, 227.89771062677553], "fontSize": 10.000003467906623},
		{"text": "higher spatial resolution, thus facilitating the acquisition", "rect": [71.96590076793323, 205.84091949462885, 291.3295399058948, 215.8409229625355], "fontSize": 10.000003467906652},
		{"text": "of multienergy images in children. These spectral capa-", "rect": [71.96590076793323, 193.8636162497781, 291.37498335404825, 203.86361971768463], "fontSize": 10.000003467906538},
		{"text": "bilities can also simplify administration of iodinated con-", "rect": [71.96590076793323, 181.8863546198064, 291.3068181818182, 191.88635808771306], "fontSize": 10.000003467906652},
		{"text": "trast media, resulting in reduced contrast agent dose and", "rect": [71.96590076793323, 169.9091033935547, 291.38634421608657, 179.9090964577415], "fontSize": 9.99999306418681},
		{"text": "rate of administration, more standardized delays to onset", "rect": [71.96590076793323, 157.8636245727539, 291.35226162997157, 167.86362804066056], "fontSize": 10.000003467906652},
		{"text": "of scanning, and decreased need for multiphase imaging.", "rect": [71.96590076793323, 145.88636294278234, 290.73862942782307, 155.88636641068888], "fontSize": 10.000003467906538},
		{"text": "PCD CT differs from conventional EID CT in the", "rect": [83.96590492942116, 133.9091013128107, 291.39772588556457, 143.9091047807173], "fontSize": 10.000003467906623},
		{"text": "mechanism by which the detector converts x-rays into the", "rect": [71.96590076793323, 121.93179806795992, 291.37498335404825, 131.93180153586644], "fontSize": 10.000003467906524},
		{"text": "signal used to construct images (1–4). In EID CT, scintil-", "rect": [71.96590076793323, 109.87501040371976, 291.38634421608657, 119.8750138716264], "fontSize": 10.000003467906637},
		{"text": "lators convert x-rays into visible light, detected by photon", "rect": [71.96590076793323, 97.89770715886898, 291.37498335404825, 107.89771062677552], "fontSize": 10.000003467906538},
		{"text": "diodes and converted into electrical signal. During the", "rect": [71.96590076793323, 85.93184800581496, 291.36362249200994, 95.9318514737216], "fontSize": 10.000003467906637},
		{"text": "transport of light photons, septa are required to prevent", "rect": [71.96590076793323, 73.95458637584339, 291.37498335404825, 83.95458984375003], "fontSize": 10.000003467906637},
		{"text": "light from scattering between detector pixels. The output", "rect": [71.96590076793323, 61.89775709672413, 291.37498335404825, 71.89776056463066], "fontSize": 10.00000346790653},
		{"text": "signal in an EID is proportional to the total energy de-", "rect": [71.96590076793323, 49.92049546675246, 291.37498335404825, 59.9204989346591], "fontSize": 10.000003467906637},
		{"text": "posited by the x-ray photons (3,4) (Fig 1A).", "rect": [71.96590076793323, 37.943150607022375, 240.9999847412109, 47.94315407492901], "fontSize": 10.000003467906637},
		{"text": "In contrast, PCD CT uses semiconductors to convert", "rect": [320.92046564275563, 421.7954781272194, 528.2841006192293, 431.7954711914062], "fontSize": 9.99999306418681},
		{"text": "x-rays to charge pairs (ie, electron and electron holes)", "rect": [308.92044067382807, 409.81817488236857, 528.3636266534978, 419.8181679465554], "fontSize": 9.99999306418681},
		{"text": "(Fig 1B). The PCD material used on the currently Food", "rect": [308.92044067382807, 397.84091325239694, 528.3522657914594, 407.84090631658376], "fontSize": 9.99999306418681},
		{"text": "and Drug Administration–approved whole-body scan-", "rect": [308.92044067382807, 385.79543443159616, 528.3863483775746, 395.7954378995028], "fontSize": 10.000003467906652},
		{"text": "ner consists of cadmium telluride. An electric field is ap-", "rect": [308.92044067382807, 373.8181728016246, 528.3068015358664, 383.8181762695312], "fontSize": 10.000003467906595},
		{"text": "plied across the semiconductor permitting the charges", "rect": [308.92044067382807, 361.8409215753728, 528.3181623979046, 371.8409146395596], "fontSize": 9.99999306418681},
		{"text": "to travel directly toward the electrodes. Septa are not re-", "rect": [308.92044067382807, 349.78408189253366, 528.3295232599431, 359.78408536044026], "fontSize": 10.000003467906595},
		{"text": "quired to prevent light scatter during this detection pro-", "rect": [308.92044067382807, 337.8068306662819, 528.3068015358664, 347.8068237304687], "fontSize": 9.99999306418681},
		{"text": "cess; this increases spatial resolution and geometric dose", "rect": [308.92044067382807, 325.8295690363103, 528.2954406738281, 335.82956210049707], "fontSize": 9.999993064186754},
		{"text": "efficiency as PCDs register the energy of each detected", "rect": [308.92044067382807, 313.85226579145944, 528.3636266534978, 323.85225885564626], "fontSize": 9.99999306418681},
		{"text": "photon (3–5). This increased geometric dose efficiency", "rect": [308.92044067382807, 301.80682858553797, 528.3636266534978, 311.80683205344457], "fontSize": 10.000003467906595},
		{"text": "underlies the capacity of PCD CT to perform similar-", "rect": [308.92044067382807, 289.8295253406871, 528.3181623979046, 299.8295288085937], "fontSize": 10.000003467906595},
		{"text": "quality studies at lower radiation doses compared with", "rect": [308.92044067382807, 277.85226371071553, 528.2840798117896, 287.8522671786221], "fontSize": 10.000003467906595},
		{"text": "EID CT, which is especially relevant in pediatric CT.", "rect": [308.92044067382807, 265.8750124844638, 518.4090770374645, 275.8750055486505], "fontSize": 9.999993064186697},
		{"text": "The energy information of individual photons re-", "rect": [320.92046564275563, 253.8181728016246, 528.3409257368608, 263.81817626953125], "fontSize": 10.000003467906652},
		{"text": "corded in the PCD CT scanner allows for more optimal", "rect": [308.92044067382807, 241.85227203369135, 528.3408841219814, 251.85227550159797], "fontSize": 10.000003467906623},
		{"text": "weighing of lower-energy photons, which increases the", "rect": [308.92044067382807, 229.87501040371978, 528.3522657914594, 239.8750138716264], "fontSize": 10.000003467906623},
		{"text": "signal of many materials, especially for iodine-enhanced", "rect": [308.92044067382807, 217.8977071588689, 528.3522657914594, 227.89771062677553], "fontSize": 10.000003467906623},
		{"text": "tissues. If the pulse signal height generated exceeds a", "rect": [308.92044067382807, 205.84091949462885, 528.3068015358664, 215.8409229625355], "fontSize": 10.000003467906652},
		{"text": "given threshold, the detected photon is counted as be-", "rect": [308.92044067382807, 193.8636162497781, 528.2954406738281, 203.86361971768463], "fontSize": 10.000003467906538},
		{"text": "longing to the corresponding threshold image (1,6–9).", "rect": [308.92044067382807, 181.8863546198064, 528.3522657914594, 191.88635808771306], "fontSize": 10.000003467906652},
		{"text": "The design also allows for a threshold to be set to exclude", "rect": [308.92044067382807, 169.9091033935547, 528.3295232599431, 179.9090964577415], "fontSize": 9.99999306418681},
		{"text": "photons less than about 20–25 keV, thereby eliminating", "rect": [308.92044067382807, 157.8636245727539, 528.3181623979046, 167.86362804066056], "fontSize": 10.000003467906652},
		{"text": "electronic noise, a feature that is particularly relevant to", "rect": [308.92044067382807, 145.88636294278234, 528.3068015358664, 155.88636641068888], "fontSize": 10.000003467906538},
		{"text": "increasing the quality of low-dose CT images obtained", "rect": [308.92044067382807, 133.9091013128107, 528.3181623979046, 143.9091047807173], "fontSize": 10.000003467906623},
		{"text": "at low photon flux, where electronic noise represents a", "rect": [308.92044067382807, 121.93179806795992, 528.3749875155361, 131.93180153586644], "fontSize": 10.000003467906524},
		{"text": "larger proportion of the detector signal (10–12). Re-", "rect": [308.92044067382807, 109.87501040371976, 528.3749875155361, 119.8750138716264], "fontSize": 10.000003467906637},
		{"text": "duction of image noise benefits pediatric CT imaging,", "rect": [308.92044067382807, 97.89770715886898, 528.3181623979046, 107.89771062677552], "fontSize": 10.000003467906538},
		{"text": "as protocols are often performed at lower radiation dose", "rect": [308.92044067382807, 85.93184800581496, 528.3181623979046, 95.9318514737216], "fontSize": 10.000003467906637},
		{"text": "exposures than in adults.", "rect": [308.92044067382807, 73.95458637584339, 404.4090791182084, 83.95458984375003], "fontSize": 10.000003467906637},
		{"text": "The first commercial whole-body PCD CT scanner", "rect": [320.92046564275563, 61.89775709672413, 528.352286598899, 71.89776056463066], "fontSize": 10.00000346790653},
		{"text": "(NAEOTOM Alpha; Siemens Healthineers) became", "rect": [308.92044067382807, 49.92049546675246, 528.3863483775746, 59.9204989346591], "fontSize": 10.000003467906637},
		{"text": "available in 2021. The terminology and protocols that", "rect": [308.92044067382807, 37.943150607022375, 528.3295232599431, 47.94315407492901], "fontSize": 10.000003467906637},
		{"text": "Performing CT in children comes with unique challenges such as greater degrees of patient motion, smaller and densely packed", "rect": [83.96590492942116, 542.4318216497246, 489.2386488481001, 550.9318167946554], "fontSize": 8.499995144930836},
		{"text": "anatomy, and potential risks of radiation exposure. The technical advancements of photon-counting detector (PCD) CT enable", "rect": [83.96590492942116, 532.95454268022, 489.61364052512425, 541.4545482288706], "fontSize": 8.50000554865062},
		{"text": "decreased radiation dose and noise, as well as increased spatial and contrast resolution across all ages, compared with conventional", "rect": [83.96590492942116, 523.4886349764737, 495.80680847167963, 531.9886405251243], "fontSize": 8.50000554865062},
		{"text": "energy-integrating detector CT. It is therefore valuable to review the relevant technical aspects and principles specific to protocol", "rect": [83.96590492942116, 513.9318091652609, 491.0909271240234, 522.4318043101918], "fontSize": 8.499995144930836},
		{"text": "development on the new PCD CT platform to realize the potential benefits for this population. The purpose of this article, based on", "rect": [83.96590492942116, 504.46592226895405, 505.78410061922926, 512.9659174138849], "fontSize": 8.499995144930836},
		{"text": "multi-institutional clinical and research experience from pediatric radiologists and medical physicists, is to provide protocol guidance", "rect": [83.96590492942116, 494.92046772349954, 505.9659160267222, 503.42046286843043], "fontSize": 8.499995144930892},
		{"text": "for use of PCD CT in the imaging of pediatric patients.", "rect": [83.96590492942116, 485.4431679465553, 261.96589383212, 493.94317349520594], "fontSize": 8.50000554865062},
		{"text": "© RSNA, 2024", "rect": [83.96590492942116, 468.86362318559117, 125.80681540749289, 475.8636308149857], "fontSize": 7.000007629394531},
		{"text": "Multi-institutional Protocol Guidance for Pediatric Photon-", "rect": [71.96590076793323, 718.238633589311, 518.5340881347655, 738.2386405251242], "fontSize": 20.00000693581319},
		{"text": "counting CT", "rect": [71.96590076793323, 696.2386363636363, 163.80680777809835, 716.2386328957297], "fontSize": 19.999996532093405},
		{"text": "Kelly K. Horst, MD", "rect": [71.96590076793323, 668.1931832053443, 143.46590215509585, 678.193186673251], "fontSize": 10.000003467906708},
		{"text": "•", "rect": [147.69318320534444, 668.1931832053443, 151.19318181818178, 678.193186673251], "fontSize": 10.000003467906708},
